# `.env` alone matches only that exact name — an `.env.bak` or a dated
# `.env.stale-backup-*` left by a tooling run is NOT ignored by it, and is one
# `git add -A` away from being committed. Cover the backup shapes explicitly.
.env.bak
.env.*.bak
.env.*backup*

